# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool
*.out

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# Compiled desktop application
/build/bin/

# Badge intermediates. Only the rewritten README.md is committed.
/build/badges/

# Frontend bundle. Generated by `npm --prefix web run build` and embedded into
# the binary at compile time. The directory itself is kept so
# that a plain `go build` on a fresh clone still satisfies the //go:embed in
# app/adapters/assets.
/app/adapters/assets/dist/*
!/app/adapters/assets/dist/.gitkeep

# Node
/web/node_modules/

# Packaging assets rendered from build/appicon.png by `wails3 generate icons`
# and from build/windows/ by `wails3 generate syso`, on every `make build`.
# Generated rather than committed for the reason the frontend bundle is: they
# are a function of a source that IS committed, and a stale binary copy of one
# is worse than no copy.
/build/darwin/iconfile.icns
/build/windows/icon.ico

# The Windows resource object `wails3 generate syso` writes beside main.go, so
# the linker picks it up. Build output, like the icons above.
*.syso

# IDE-specific files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS-specific files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db

# Log files
*.log
